(2548916, 350112, 54172, '<td valign="top">Nice photo. You have a solid background color, which i guess is out of focus, because the petal in the background is also out of focus. I do like the photo very much, but I don''t think that this is a clear case of bokeh, but that doesn''t mean that it is not. After looking at this again, I reconsidered my score.<br/> <br/>One thing I would change in this photo is get rid of the things in the background on the righ edge, and bottom right corner - they are a little distracting</td>', 'Nice photo. You have a solid background color, which i guess is out of focus, because the petal in the background is also out of focus. I do like the photo very much, but I don''t think that this is a clear case of bokeh, but that doesn''t mean that it is not. After looking at this again, I reconsidered my score. One thing I would change in this photo is get rid of the things in the background on the righ edge, and bottom right corner - they are a little distracting', '2006-06-24 15:29:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2548921, 349666, 39900, '<td valign="top">Great shot 7</td>', 'Great shot 7', '2006-06-24 15:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2548924, 349575, 39900, '<td valign="top">Omg what a great shot this is. I like the focus.<br/>This i sthe top 10 here in this challenge maby ribbon :P <br/>ill give u 8</td>', 'Omg what a great shot this is. I like the focus.This i sthe top 10 here in this challenge maby ribbon :P ill give u 8', '2006-06-24 15:35:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2548943, 349709, 57260, '<td valign="top">Ok, the idea could definately work but you need your subject (the hand holding the apple) to be in sharp focus and fill more of the frame, to draw attention to it and an even shallower DOP to blur the background. Also her fingers are burnt from too harsh lighting, so I would try and use a softer light source and move it off even more to one side and concentrate it on the apple and less on the person in the background since that distracts from the subject. Hope that helps</td>', 'Ok, the idea could definately work but you need your subject (the hand holding the apple) to be in sharp focus and fill more of the frame, to draw attention to it and an even shallower DOP to blur the background. Also her fingers are burnt from too harsh lighting, so I would try and use a softer light source and move it off even more to one side and concentrate it on the apple and less on the person in the background since that distracts from the subject. Hope that helps', '2006-06-24 15:54:07.000000', NULL, 1),
