(2557216, 350542, 41337, '<td valign="top">Nice take to the challenge however the image needs some post editing work, IMO. The two problems for me is the low contrast and the low saturation. To fix this in photoshop I would use a Curves adjustment (click "options" and then "enhance per channel contrast" and then ok). Then I would use unsharp mask to boost the local contrast (i.e. settings similar to this: Amount=16, Radius=25, Threshold=1). This would make the image pop more both in color and contrast. This still won''t get the white on the eagle''s head whiter like it should so maybe also use Replace Color, which is under "Images/Adjustments" menu and use the eyedropper tool on the eagles head and then bump up the "Lightness" slider a bit to make it brighter. If you choose the right spot you will miminize brightening the white in the background. <br/> <br/>Anyway, just some suggestions on improving this particular shot. If you were to reshoot I would suggest getting much lower and shooting up a bit so that you only got the blue background with the stars. That way you would avoid the bright white stripe which is a bit of a distraction, IMO.</td>', 'Nice take to the challenge however the image needs some post editing work, IMO. The two problems for me is the low contrast and the low saturation. To fix this in photoshop I would use a Curves adjustment (click "options" and then "enhance per channel contrast" and then ok). Then I would use unsharp mask to boost the local contrast (i.e. settings similar to this: Amount=16, Radius=25, Threshold=1). This would make the image pop more both in color and contrast. This still won''t get the white on the eagle''s head whiter like it should so maybe also use Replace Color, which is under "Images/Adjustments" menu and use the eyedropper tool on the eagles head and then bump up the "Lightness" slider a bit to make it brighter. If you choose the right spot you will miminize brightening the white in the background.  Anyway, just some suggestions on improving this particular shot. If you were to reshoot I would suggest getting much lower and shooting up a bit so that you only got the blue background with the stars. That way you would avoid the bright white stripe which is a bit of a distraction, IMO.', '2006-06-27 04:09:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2557255, 349464, 35274, '<td valign="top">Heyz! I knew I would find it eventually :-P I like the composition and it''s a fine example of proper bokeh. Parrots always make for an interesting subject ;-) The highlights seem a tad bright, tho it might just be my monitor. Hope this does well, good luck! :-D</td>', 'Heyz! I knew I would find it eventually :-P I like the composition and it''s a fine example of proper bokeh. Parrots always make for an interesting subject ;-) The highlights seem a tad bright, tho it might just be my monitor. Hope this does well, good luck! :-D', '2006-06-27 05:18:01.000000', NULL, 1),
