(2561893, 348584, 20168, '<td valign="top">Lovely photo Jason! Congrats on another DPC blue!</td>', 'Lovely photo Jason! Congrats on another DPC blue!', '2006-06-28 12:35:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2561929, 349476, 29156, '<td valign="top">very good capture and great colors</td>', 'very good capture and great colors', '2006-06-28 12:41:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2561944, 350806, 40718, '<td valign="top">Two things I think could have gotten you closer to 6.<br/>1) Less centered.  So that means zoom back and leave some negative space on one side (likely the right in this shot).<br/>2) Change the composition to reveal more of the "cup" of the flower.  Doesn''t have to be all the way, but I feel like we want more.<br/> <br/>The bokeh is nicely done, especially for a P&amp;S.  The lighting is nice. The colors are nice too, although I think the greens look just a tad dull.  I''d have to goof in PS though to see how to improve that.</td>', 'Two things I think could have gotten you closer to 6.1) Less centered.  So that means zoom back and leave some negative space on one side (likely the right in this shot).2) Change the composition to reveal more of the "cup" of the flower.  Doesn''t have to be all the way, but I feel like we want more. The bokeh is nicely done, especially for a P&S.  The lighting is nice. The colors are nice too, although I think the greens look just a tad dull.  I''d have to goof in PS though to see how to improve that.', '2006-06-28 12:43:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562008, 350865, 40718, '<td valign="top">Well, you certainly have bokeh in this shot. ;)  Two things.  I think the entries that did best had a completely focused subject while having a very unfocused background.  Not to say that you have to do it that way, but I think the OOF portion of your subject hurt you a bit.  The second also relates.  Look at the four leaves above the sharp one.  I noticed these when I voted and didn''t like their haloing.  It could totally be your lens (or it may be PP), but I would call this "bad" bokeh.  The rest of the shot is pleasant, but those four leaves made me give you a 5.</td>', 'Well, you certainly have bokeh in this shot. ;)  Two things.  I think the entries that did best had a completely focused subject while having a very unfocused background.  Not to say that you have to do it that way, but I think the OOF portion of your subject hurt you a bit.  The second also relates.  Look at the four leaves above the sharp one.  I noticed these when I voted and didn''t like their haloing.  It could totally be your lens (or it may be PP), but I would call this "bad" bokeh.  The rest of the shot is pleasant, but those four leaves made me give you a 5.', '2006-06-28 12:57:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562017, 349697, 51538, '<td valign="top">Congrats!  A great image and a nice finish...  I was thinking yours was the Kookah!</td>', 'Congrats!  A great image and a nice finish...  I was thinking yours was the Kookah!', '2006-06-28 13:00:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562022, 350567, 51538, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot, was a 10 for me.</td>', 'Wonderful shot, was a 10 for me.', '2006-06-28 13:00:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562030, 350068, 51538, '<td valign="top">Good work on the transition away from Aloe ;-)</td>', 'Good work on the transition away from Aloe ;-)', '2006-06-28 13:02:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562033, 348989, 51538, '<td valign="top">There you go again.  Your work always has a quality to it.</td>', 'There you go again.  Your work always has a quality to it.', '2006-06-28 13:03:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562054, 350844, 40718, '<td valign="top">Hey! Another butterfly shot.  I gave this a 6 when I came through originally.  6 to me is a solid shot so I think you are a bit underrated.<br/> <br/>I think what hurt you the most is the razor thin DOF.  It was a real balancing act in this challenge.  The best shots managed to keep most of the subject in focus while having the background still all "bokehed up".  When I took my shots, I would find a subject and then fire off with my finger on the dial for changing the aperture.  I started at 4 and then would work my way up in maybe 2/3rd steps to about 8.  Then I''d sort it out later.<br/> <br/>Colors and composition are nice.  What IS in focus is sharp and nicely done.  The flowers are just a bit blown.</td>', 'Hey! Another butterfly shot.  I gave this a 6 when I came through originally.  6 to me is a solid shot so I think you are a bit underrated. I think what hurt you the most is the razor thin DOF.  It was a real balancing act in this challenge.  The best shots managed to keep most of the subject in focus while having the background still all "bokehed up".  When I took my shots, I would find a subject and then fire off with my finger on the dial for changing the aperture.  I started at 4 and then would work my way up in maybe 2/3rd steps to about 8.  Then I''d sort it out later. Colors and composition are nice.  What IS in focus is sharp and nicely done.  The flowers are just a bit blown.', '2006-06-28 13:08:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562059, 350113, 37961, '<td valign="top">I bet that smelled good! So Pretty too.</td>', 'I bet that smelled good! So Pretty too.', '2006-06-28 13:08:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562096, 348316, 51750, '<td valign="top">Matt good job with this one, my entry in this challenge was my worst one ever, but superstions is making up for it<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-28 12:17:29.</i></td>', 'Matt good job with this one, my entry in this challenge was my worst one ever, but superstions is making up for it', '2006-06-28 13:16:49.000000', '2006-06-28 13:17:29.000000', 0),
(2562116, 348346, 19670, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot and gave it an 8. I don''t think it''s unusual that it''s been selected as a fav more than most top 10 finishers. Some probably had difficulty in figuring out how to vote for this challenge topic, but still liked your shot as a beautiful visual, challenge or no.</td>', 'I liked this shot and gave it an 8. I don''t think it''s unusual that it''s been selected as a fav more than most top 10 finishers. Some probably had difficulty in figuring out how to vote for this challenge topic, but still liked your shot as a beautiful visual, challenge or no.', '2006-06-28 13:20:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562177, 348316, 35545, '<td valign="top">Weird and wonderful.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-28 15:54:33.</i></td>', 'Weird and wonderful.', '2006-06-28 13:40:23.000000', '2006-06-28 16:54:33.000000', 0),
(2562199, 348346, 49672, '<td valign="top">I was one of the four 9s - for me it was the superbly creamy bokeh (yes, of course it *is* bokeh!) but also it was pretty bold to submit such an abstract shot in this challenge.  It really stood out against the other flower shots, mine included.</td>', 'I was one of the four 9s - for me it was the superbly creamy bokeh (yes, of course it *is* bokeh!) but also it was pretty bold to submit such an abstract shot in this challenge.  It really stood out against the other flower shots, mine included.', '2006-06-28 13:46:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562252, 348584, 30861, '<td valign="top">Excellent! This struck me from the get-go! Congrats!</td>', 'Excellent! This struck me from the get-go! Congrats!', '2006-06-28 13:59:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562257, 349697, 29011, '<td valign="top">Perfect stop action shot of a bee in flight. Beautiful bokeh and color. Congratulations :)</td>', 'Perfect stop action shot of a bee in flight. Beautiful bokeh and color. Congratulations :)', '2006-06-28 14:00:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562263, 349217, 30861, '<td valign="top">Oh, fantastic. This was one of my top-scorers anyway, and now that I see the setup and all, I''m just amazed! Congrats on ribbon!</td>', 'Oh, fantastic. This was one of my top-scorers anyway, and now that I see the setup and all, I''m just amazed! Congrats on ribbon!', '2006-06-28 14:02:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562265, 349217, 29011, '<td valign="top">Great job with the setup! very creative. My favorite non bird/bug shot of the challenge.</td>', 'Great job with the setup! very creative. My favorite non bird/bug shot of the challenge.', '2006-06-28 14:02:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562268, 350711, 44099, '<td valign="top">Bah...I was hoping to do a little better with this pic. I really like it. Oh well, photography is subjective, so it doesn''t really matter. Thanks for the comments.</td>', 'Bah...I was hoping to do a little better with this pic. I really like it. Oh well, photography is subjective, so it doesn''t really matter. Thanks for the comments.', '2006-06-28 14:02:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562274, 350413, 29011, '<td valign="top">Magical capture. Amazingly creative yet simple image. Really thought this one would place better. Most of the spoon being OOF wasn''t a big deal for me.</td>', 'Magical capture. Amazingly creative yet simple image. Really thought this one would place better. Most of the spoon being OOF wasn''t a big deal for me.', '2006-06-28 14:04:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562295, 349697, 30861, '<td valign="top">WTG dude! Very nice work!</td>', 'WTG dude! Very nice work!', '2006-06-28 14:10:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562298, 350567, 30861, '<td valign="top">How nice to see a kookaburra do so well! Congrats on the high finish!</td>', 'How nice to see a kookaburra do so well! Congrats on the high finish!', '2006-06-28 14:11:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562306, 349308, 30861, '<td valign="top">Nicely done! Sweet, peaceful bokeh!</td>', 'Nicely done! Sweet, peaceful bokeh!', '2006-06-28 14:13:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562310, 348584, 19670, '<td valign="top">Congratulations. I love the clarity of the butterfly, and the green and purple colors in the background.</td>', 'Congratulations. I love the clarity of the butterfly, and the green and purple colors in the background.', '2006-06-28 14:14:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562338, 350413, 5112, '<td valign="top">Thank you all very much, all the comments are much appreciated.<br/> <br/>As for most of the spoon being out of focus, I call it "artistic license".  I like it that way :)  All I wanted in focus is the tip and a bit of the rim of the spoon, the handle and the back/inside were supposed to be out of focus, the handle has bokeh circles on it.  <br/> <br/>He, he, I guess that goes to show that artistic license isn''t going to get me anywhere here.  Oh well.<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-28 14:39:07.</i></td>', 'Thank you all very much, all the comments are much appreciated. As for most of the spoon being out of focus, I call it "artistic license".  I like it that way :)  All I wanted in focus is the tip and a bit of the rim of the spoon, the handle and the back/inside were supposed to be out of focus, the handle has bokeh circles on it.   He, he, I guess that goes to show that artistic license isn''t going to get me anywhere here.  Oh well. ', '2006-06-28 14:22:01.000000', '2006-06-28 15:39:07.000000', 0),
(2562352, 349217, 51889, '<td valign="top">This truly deserved to ribbon! You were very creative with the setup :)<br/></td>', 'This truly deserved to ribbon! You were very creative with the setup :)', '2006-06-28 14:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562353, 351022, 40718, '<td valign="top">4.58?  This was underrated.  I would have guessed 5.3 or so at least.  It''s a nice shot.  Very abstract, which isn''t bad, but doesn''t always fly on DPC.  The bokeh is, to the purist, "bad" but only because of your lens and not because of your shot.  On the other hand, those little donuts are sorta cool.  Lends to the abstract quality.<br/> <br/>In composition, I would have shifted the field of view a little to the left so as to have a bit more of the space behind the vase.  I think it''s a tad cramped over there as it is.<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote this one in the challenge, but I would have likely given it a 5 or 6, so I think you got robbed a bit. ;)</td>', '4.58?  This was underrated.  I would have guessed 5.3 or so at least.  It''s a nice shot.  Very abstract, which isn''t bad, but doesn''t always fly on DPC.  The bokeh is, to the purist, "bad" but only because of your lens and not because of your shot.  On the other hand, those little donuts are sorta cool.  Lends to the abstract quality. In composition, I would have shifted the field of view a little to the left so as to have a bit more of the space behind the vase.  I think it''s a tad cramped over there as it is. I didn''t vote this one in the challenge, but I would have likely given it a 5 or 6, so I think you got robbed a bit. ;)', '2006-06-28 14:27:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562368, 351015, 40718, '<td valign="top">A few thoughts:<br/>1) The subject doesn''t take up enough of the canvas.  I would have included more or zoomed more so the current amount shown takes up more space.<br/>2) The picture is just a tad on the dark side for a flower shot.  I would have tried to boost midtones to pull it up a bit.<br/>3) The part of the bokeh that bothers me is the halo effect on the orange in the background.  It doesn''t look good to me.  You have a nice lens, so I''m not sure where that came from.  Maybe the extension tube.</td>', 'A few thoughts:1) The subject doesn''t take up enough of the canvas.  I would have included more or zoomed more so the current amount shown takes up more space.2) The picture is just a tad on the dark side for a flower shot.  I would have tried to boost midtones to pull it up a bit.3) The part of the bokeh that bothers me is the halo effect on the orange in the background.  It doesn''t look good to me.  You have a nice lens, so I''m not sure where that came from.  Maybe the extension tube.', '2006-06-28 14:33:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562388, 350711, 40718, '<td valign="top">I like the 50mm/1.8 as a lens a lot.  Just be aware that at 1.8 it can be soft.  You can see that in this shot.  Look at the knobs on the violin.  DPC loves sharp, sharp, sharp.  It also looks like you or the camera chose to focus on the far right and the ornamental hole (ya, ok, I don''t know the parts of a violin by name).  I would have focused on either those knobs I spoke of or the strings.<br/> <br/>The bokeh is nice, but has a bit of an issue.  The two straight lines don''t add anything to the composition informationally so they just wind up distracting.</td>', 'I like the 50mm/1.8 as a lens a lot.  Just be aware that at 1.8 it can be soft.  You can see that in this shot.  Look at the knobs on the violin.  DPC loves sharp, sharp, sharp.  It also looks like you or the camera chose to focus on the far right and the ornamental hole (ya, ok, I don''t know the parts of a violin by name).  I would have focused on either those knobs I spoke of or the strings. The bokeh is nice, but has a bit of an issue.  The two straight lines don''t add anything to the composition informationally so they just wind up distracting.', '2006-06-28 14:37:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562434, 349415, 43519, '<td valign="top">This picture should have got a ribbon...In my opinion, your submission is far better than some winner pictures. Do not pay attention very much to the score. Great job!</td>', 'This picture should have got a ribbon...In my opinion, your submission is far better than some winner pictures. Do not pay attention very much to the score. Great job!', '2006-06-28 14:48:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562485, 350060, 40718, '<td valign="top">You have some things going for the shot here.  I like the leading line and the composition.  The bokeh is nice.  I think the biggest think here is the tones are very cool.  Flowers, mainly, like warm and cheery tones.  Banmorn may have something to say about that, but in an outdoor, non-studio shot, I would go for warmth.  That''s really my biggest beef with the shot.<br/> <br/>If I changed anything else, I may recompose just a bit.  I''m not quite sure about the flowers trailing out of the frame.  Perhaps it would have been better if they ended before the edge.  Would have to see it though...</td>', 'You have some things going for the shot here.  I like the leading line and the composition.  The bokeh is nice.  I think the biggest think here is the tones are very cool.  Flowers, mainly, like warm and cheery tones.  Banmorn may have something to say about that, but in an outdoor, non-studio shot, I would go for warmth.  That''s really my biggest beef with the shot. If I changed anything else, I may recompose just a bit.  I''m not quite sure about the flowers trailing out of the frame.  Perhaps it would have been better if they ended before the edge.  Would have to see it though...', '2006-06-28 15:01:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562493, 347774, 40370, '<td valign="top">5.8 is a great average but I can''t believe 83rd place, much too low for this wonderful image. I agree with pinapple, maybe a dark background might have helped the bokeh, but still you made a "point". Gave you a 10.</td>', '5.8 is a great average but I can''t believe 83rd place, much too low for this wonderful image. I agree with pinapple, maybe a dark background might have helped the bokeh, but still you made a "point". Gave you a 10.', '2006-06-28 15:02:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562506, 350417, 40718, '<td valign="top">Really I think above 5.5 most shots show a basic grasp of all the techincals needed for a good picture.  Then it becomes a matter of subject, "wow" and the small details that raise it above.<br/> <br/>I have always found reds to be very hard to control on the Canon sensor.  They saturate very very quickly and can look bad.  I took a bunch of tulip shots in April and had the exact same problem.  This shot may be suffering from that a bit.  Try actually desaturating the reds a small amount and see if it looks better. (we rarely think of desaturating things unless we are going for selective desat or B&amp;W).<br/> <br/>The bokeh is mainly nice, but I think the lawn section is blown a bit which makes it less appealing.  I also don''t quite like the two horizontal highlights.  Because it makes a pattern, our eyes are drawn to it and away from the subject.  It doesn''t add to the picture informationally, so it just winds up being a distraction.</td>', 'Really I think above 5.5 most shots show a basic grasp of all the techincals needed for a good picture.  Then it becomes a matter of subject, "wow" and the small details that raise it above. I have always found reds to be very hard to control on the Canon sensor.  They saturate very very quickly and can look bad.  I took a bunch of tulip shots in April and had the exact same problem.  This shot may be suffering from that a bit.  Try actually desaturating the reds a small amount and see if it looks better. (we rarely think of desaturating things unless we are going for selective desat or B&W). The bokeh is mainly nice, but I think the lawn section is blown a bit which makes it less appealing.  I also don''t quite like the two horizontal highlights.  Because it makes a pattern, our eyes are drawn to it and away from the subject.  It doesn''t add to the picture informationally, so it just winds up being a distraction.', '2006-06-28 15:05:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2562516, 348584, 36060, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon! Great shot!</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon! Great shot!', '2006-06-28 15:07:35.000000', NULL, 0),
