(2566385, 349276, 38496, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favs.  I love the title, and the grey bokeh background makes the guy really ''pop''.  The ligthing on the rooster is great;  the feather detail really nice.  I like the way his beak is open, so that you can hear him saying "Cock-a-bokeh-do".<br/>Nice Job!</td>', 'This was one of my favs.  I love the title, and the grey bokeh background makes the guy really ''pop''.  The ligthing on the rooster is great;  the feather detail really nice.  I like the way his beak is open, so that you can hear him saying "Cock-a-bokeh-do".Nice Job!', '2006-06-29 14:11:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2566405, 349561, 50741, '<td valign="top">great shot  well done</td>', 'great shot  well done', '2006-06-29 14:19:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2566450, 350430, 13077, '<td valign="top">Overall, it''s a pretty nice portrait. I know how it feels to get a way lower score than you expect, but if the client is happy it''s OK, right?<br/> <br/>The technical things that mk mentioned are true, and I wouldn''t mind seeing a little more contrast and sharpness on the face. Maybe try a little smaller radius with USM, there are some small halo issues going on.<br/> <br/>Also, expect to be scored based on the model when you enter portraits... it might not be your fault that the model''s eyes seem to face different directions or that she''s overweight, but people will score it lower if it annoys them.</td>', 'Overall, it''s a pretty nice portrait. I know how it feels to get a way lower score than you expect, but if the client is happy it''s OK, right? The technical things that mk mentioned are true, and I wouldn''t mind seeing a little more contrast and sharpness on the face. Maybe try a little smaller radius with USM, there are some small halo issues going on. Also, expect to be scored based on the model when you enter portraits... it might not be your fault that the model''s eyes seem to face different directions or that she''s overweight, but people will score it lower if it annoys them.', '2006-06-29 14:31:53.000000', NULL, 0),
