(2567819, 350451, 32997, '<td valign="top">I think this deserved a MUCH higher score..but am sure that people didn''t really like the b &amp; w...<br/>the background being so insignificant is probably what did you in..don''t get defeated by this score...<br/>I like your creative approach..</td>', 'I think this deserved a MUCH higher score..but am sure that people didn''t really like the b & w...the background being so insignificant is probably what did you in..don''t get defeated by this score...I like your creative approach..', '2006-06-29 23:01:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2567852, 350362, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Tres cool shot!  Definitely meets the challenge.  I like the detail you can see in the little guys "face" and the bokeh very much works here - clever idea to "create" that bokeh, too.  To make it better?  Maybe a bit sharper on the damselfly, but working with that close a macro, I''m not entirely sure how you''d do that.  I''ve yet to even try anything that close, but I''m pretty sure it ain''t easy.  Well done, and underrated.<br/> <br/>OK, just peeked - I see you got a comment from the good Doc.  :-)</td>', 'Trading Post comment Tres cool shot!  Definitely meets the challenge.  I like the detail you can see in the little guys "face" and the bokeh very much works here - clever idea to "create" that bokeh, too.  To make it better?  Maybe a bit sharper on the damselfly, but working with that close a macro, I''m not entirely sure how you''d do that.  I''ve yet to even try anything that close, but I''m pretty sure it ain''t easy.  Well done, and underrated. OK, just peeked - I see you got a comment from the good Doc.  :-)', '2006-06-29 23:13:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2567865, 350672, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Great flower shot!  A challenge too early... :-)  Works for this one, too, though with such a tight crop, the bokeh doesn''t emphasize the flower as much as it could if the crop were a bit wider.  That said, this is an excellent shot - the color is very rich and warm without being overly bright or oversaturated; the focus is excellent; and I like the composition.  It''s not quite the rule of thirds, but for me, the bud on the right of the bloom balances it nicely.</td>', 'Trading Post comment Great flower shot!  A challenge too early... :-)  Works for this one, too, though with such a tight crop, the bokeh doesn''t emphasize the flower as much as it could if the crop were a bit wider.  That said, this is an excellent shot - the color is very rich and warm without being overly bright or oversaturated; the focus is excellent; and I like the composition.  It''s not quite the rule of thirds, but for me, the bud on the right of the bloom balances it nicely.', '2006-06-29 23:16:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2567887, 349569, 34013, '<td valign="top">this is simply amazing. the color sat is perfect, the framing is perfect. very well done!</td>', 'this is simply amazing. the color sat is perfect, the framing is perfect. very well done!', '2006-06-29 23:19:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2567895, 350164, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>This did pretty well for a flower shot!  :-)  Love the crisp focus on the foreground flower and nice choice of subject as that''s a particularly lovely bloom.  The bee is a welcome addition as it adds interest but you should have convinced him to fly into the picture rather than out of it - doesn''t he understand the rules of composition?  Well lit, good color, and nice bokeh to boot.</td>', 'Trading Post comment This did pretty well for a flower shot!  :-)  Love the crisp focus on the foreground flower and nice choice of subject as that''s a particularly lovely bloom.  The bee is a welcome addition as it adds interest but you should have convinced him to fly into the picture rather than out of it - doesn''t he understand the rules of composition?  Well lit, good color, and nice bokeh to boot.', '2006-06-29 23:21:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2567930, 349697, 36371, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! I gave this a 10. It was magical! And now it''s a favorite in my portfolio! Thanks!</td>', 'Congratulations! I gave this a 10. It was magical! And now it''s a favorite in my portfolio! Thanks!', '2006-06-29 23:29:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2567976, 349697, 47294, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  Great shot - really stunning.  Great to see you with another ribbon.  Go Aussie!  <br/> <br/>Nic.</td>', 'Congratulations!  Great shot - really stunning.  Great to see you with another ribbon.  Go Aussie!   Nic.', '2006-06-29 23:40:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568138, 350882, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - I did not vote in this challenge but probabaly would have gone with a 5. You definitley met the challenge with the background bokeh but the pic as a whole does not seem to stand out. Not much color going and with the white flower I think it could have used some more green standing out to frame it in better. Possibly isolating 3 flower heads totally in the shot rather than have a couple of them leaving the frame could have helped with the overall composition. Again - not a bad shot, just not a standout either.</td>', 'Trading Post - I did not vote in this challenge but probabaly would have gone with a 5. You definitley met the challenge with the background bokeh but the pic as a whole does not seem to stand out. Not much color going and with the white flower I think it could have used some more green standing out to frame it in better. Possibly isolating 3 flower heads totally in the shot rather than have a couple of them leaving the frame could have helped with the overall composition. Again - not a bad shot, just not a standout either.', '2006-06-30 01:00:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568145, 350621, 3724, '<td valign="top">......soft pastels to vivid - interesting and very good.</td>', '......soft pastels to vivid - interesting and very good.', '2006-06-30 01:05:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568153, 350672, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - Not a bad flower shot, but the crop really pevents the background bokeh to have any impact on the flower itself. Good color and general detail in the flower head. I think if you had pulled back though to see more of the background you would have scored higher.</td>', 'Trading Post - Not a bad flower shot, but the crop really pevents the background bokeh to have any impact on the flower itself. Good color and general detail in the flower head. I think if you had pulled back though to see more of the background you would have scored higher.', '2006-06-30 01:07:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568162, 350362, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - Way to go on setting up the shot to bring in more color and have more attention brought to the background bokeh. Great thinking. I did not vote in this challenge but probably would have gone a 6. I would have scored it much higher had more of the bug been in focus. Great combination of colors though a slight sat adjustment on the green to bring it out a bit more would hav ebeen nice.</td>', 'Trading Post - Way to go on setting up the shot to bring in more color and have more attention brought to the background bokeh. Great thinking. I did not vote in this challenge but probably would have gone a 6. I would have scored it much higher had more of the bug been in focus. Great combination of colors though a slight sat adjustment on the green to bring it out a bit more would hav ebeen nice.', '2006-06-30 01:12:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568193, 350164, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - Not a bad shot. Way to go on catching a flying bee. I think if you could have caught him in focus and had the flower be your bokeh in front you may have scored some more points. Nice colors and the background bokeh works pretty good. I think the crop may be just a tad bit too tight as I think I would have liked to have seen the whole head of the flower in the shot.</td>', 'Trading Post - Not a bad shot. Way to go on catching a flying bee. I think if you could have caught him in focus and had the flower be your bokeh in front you may have scored some more points. Nice colors and the background bokeh works pretty good. I think the crop may be just a tad bit too tight as I think I would have liked to have seen the whole head of the flower in the shot.', '2006-06-30 01:23:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568245, 348340, 45318, '<td valign="top">point taken as far as the iffy bokeh!</td>', 'point taken as far as the iffy bokeh!', '2006-06-30 01:44:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568257, 349764, 41008, '<td valign="top">I think this picture is absolutely gorgeous and should have scored much higher than it did.</td>', 'I think this picture is absolutely gorgeous and should have scored much higher than it did.', '2006-06-30 01:48:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568731, 348584, 29658, '<td valign="top">Hey Doc,<br/> <br/>this is wonderful.</td>', 'Hey Doc, this is wonderful.', '2006-06-30 04:38:43.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2568836, 351022, 46314, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i>I think you got robbed a bit. ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Robbed. Definitely. This shot really tackled the challenge well. Because it''s abstract, I think a lot of people simply dismiss it immediately. <br/>But if you give yourself a little time to look at it, it really draws you in.<br/>Never got around to voting on it, but I like it. Definitely would have rated it higher than it got.<br/>Keep trying.</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo:I think you got robbed a bit. ;)   Robbed. Definitely. This shot really tackled the challenge well. Because it''s abstract, I think a lot of people simply dismiss it immediately. But if you give yourself a little time to look at it, it really draws you in.Never got around to voting on it, but I like it. Definitely would have rated it higher than it got.Keep trying.', '2006-06-30 06:33:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2568953, 348584, 24073, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Doc.  I really like this one, I was the other butterfly that scored 14th.  Though I liked mine alot, I liked this one much more.  Its seems brighter, happier, and crisper.  Executed very nicely with a beautiful Bokeh.  Well deserving!</td>', 'Congratulations Doc.  I really like this one, I was the other butterfly that scored 14th.  Though I liked mine alot, I liked this one much more.  Its seems brighter, happier, and crisper.  Executed very nicely with a beautiful Bokeh.  Well deserving!', '2006-06-30 08:46:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2569125, 349191, 30049, '<td valign="top">Just for the record.  I didn''t vote on this, or any image, in the Bokeh II challenge.<br/> <br/>To clear up any misquotes used in user profiles (<i>"...told me that they scored my image low because the hands of the subject were cut off."</i>), what was said exactly is this:<br/> <br/><b>Originally posted by specialk0783:</b> <br/> <br/>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br/><i>... There is a picture of a deer that came in (71st I think?) - that the bg is almost completely blurred a solid color...no nothing...71st? Over my image? ... <br/> <br/>... When a completely blurred, nearly solid color bg gets 71st in a bokeh challenge and my entry gets 201st....I just can''t possibly be happy with the voters.  </i> <br/> <br/><b>Originally posted response by glad2badad:</b> <br/> <br/>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br/><i>It appears that some people prefer a deer as the subject to 1 1/2 hands? ;^)</i> <br/> <br/>The entire forum thread can be viewed here: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=417169&amp;page=3" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Bokeh Placement - Please tell me if underrated?</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-30 09:29:05.</i></td>', 'Just for the record.  I didn''t vote on this, or any image, in the Bokeh II challenge. To clear up any misquotes used in user profiles ("...told me that they scored my image low because the hands of the subject were cut off."), what was said exactly is this: Originally posted by specialk0783:  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------... There is a picture of a deer that came in (71st I think?) - that the bg is almost completely blurred a solid color...no nothing...71st? Over my image? ...  ... When a completely blurred, nearly solid color bg gets 71st in a bokeh challenge and my entry gets 201st....I just can''t possibly be happy with the voters.    Originally posted response by glad2badad:  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------It appears that some people prefer a deer as the subject to 1 1/2 hands? ;^)  The entire forum thread can be viewed here: Bokeh Placement - Please tell me if underrated?', '2006-06-30 10:19:09.000000', '2006-06-30 10:29:05.000000', 0),
