(2583716, 349697, 17203, '<td valign="top">I knew this would ribbon the first time I saw it. I probably would have cropped more off the right side, but color, focus, DOF, and image appeal are all first rate. Congrats!</td>', 'I knew this would ribbon the first time I saw it. I probably would have cropped more off the right side, but color, focus, DOF, and image appeal are all first rate. Congrats!', '2006-07-04 12:36:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584534, 350210, 8367, '<td valign="top">Great job and score! :)</td>', 'Great job and score! :)', '2006-07-04 16:30:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584718, 347683, 19959, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Self portraits are never easy. This is an effective self portrait with interesting lighting and an unusual pose.<br/>The Challenge was to illustrate the effect of Bokeh and your shot does not do that.<br/> <br/>Getting good Bokeh effect is as much about the lens and camera as well as good Depth of field. (shallow) the out of focus background needs also to be presented by a pattern that blurs well into interesting abstracts for example water drops glistening in sunlight.<br/> <br/>The wood pattern on your bed board might look OK in stronger light with a deeper depth of field.<br/> <br/>Chris<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Self portraits are never easy. This is an effective self portrait with interesting lighting and an unusual pose.The Challenge was to illustrate the effect of Bokeh and your shot does not do that. Getting good Bokeh effect is as much about the lens and camera as well as good Depth of field. (shallow) the out of focus background needs also to be presented by a pattern that blurs well into interesting abstracts for example water drops glistening in sunlight. The wood pattern on your bed board might look OK in stronger light with a deeper depth of field. Chris ', '2006-07-04 18:03:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584730, 350222, 31133, '<td valign="top">Ah, I wish you would tell us how you did this in the photog comment area. I would love to learn. This is stunning.</td>', 'Ah, I wish you would tell us how you did this in the photog comment area. I would love to learn. This is stunning.', '2006-07-04 18:06:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584795, 348815, 19959, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/>Interesting photo. I really like the style of your photography, you have an alternative aproach that is quite refreshing. <br/> <br/>This is a good example of Bokeh, but did not score well with the voters, why?<br/>The idea of having the jar of PB in the background as the Bokeh is good but just doesn''t quite work. I think that perhaps in the few seconds that each voter takes to view a shot they would miss this and see a background that looks a little ''busy'' this is a shame as you certainly embraced the challenge and as some voters point out Kudos for bucking the obvious route of birds and flowers!<br/> <br/>Minor niggles are that the bread is slightly over exposed and the tray pattern is unnecessary and a little distracting. Perhaps including the whole sandwhich and making the ingedients a little more obvious would help.<br/> <br/>Overall I like it and I like your other entries (especially the green cocktail) keep up the great work and don''t let anyone tell you what to do... you have a nice style and good eye for a picture.<br/> <br/>Regards<br/> <br/>Chris (Pixelstate)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.Interesting photo. I really like the style of your photography, you have an alternative aproach that is quite refreshing.  This is a good example of Bokeh, but did not score well with the voters, why?The idea of having the jar of PB in the background as the Bokeh is good but just doesn''t quite work. I think that perhaps in the few seconds that each voter takes to view a shot they would miss this and see a background that looks a little ''busy'' this is a shame as you certainly embraced the challenge and as some voters point out Kudos for bucking the obvious route of birds and flowers! Minor niggles are that the bread is slightly over exposed and the tray pattern is unnecessary and a little distracting. Perhaps including the whole sandwhich and making the ingedients a little more obvious would help. Overall I like it and I like your other entries (especially the green cocktail) keep up the great work and don''t let anyone tell you what to do... you have a nice style and good eye for a picture. Regards Chris (Pixelstate)', '2006-07-04 18:22:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584832, 350809, 19959, '<td valign="top">Hi Jennifer<br/>Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>This is an excellent entry for the Bokeh Challenge. You have shown excellent technique and a good choice of DOF and Lens.<br/> <br/>The challenge is hard as it requires finding Bokeh to compliment the main subject which you have done perfectly. The Exposure and colors are also spot on.<br/> <br/>The overall score is fairly dissapointing, I think mainly because the bird appears slightly out of focus. Voters can be very unforgiving on this point. I suspect as Ozerion mentions that some softness has crept in through re-sizing for the challenge. It is also very useful to get a catch light in the eyes of the subject if possible, as these are the centre of attention they need to have interest.<br/> <br/>Regards<br/> <br/>Chris</td>', 'Hi JenniferGreetings from the Critique Club. This is an excellent entry for the Bokeh Challenge. You have shown excellent technique and a good choice of DOF and Lens. The challenge is hard as it requires finding Bokeh to compliment the main subject which you have done perfectly. The Exposure and colors are also spot on. The overall score is fairly dissapointing, I think mainly because the bird appears slightly out of focus. Voters can be very unforgiving on this point. I suspect as Ozerion mentions that some softness has crept in through re-sizing for the challenge. It is also very useful to get a catch light in the eyes of the subject if possible, as these are the centre of attention they need to have interest. Regards Chris', '2006-07-04 18:31:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584858, 349217, 3419, '<td valign="top">Wow! You sure had me fooled. I thought it was a natural nature scene! Good job!</td>', 'Wow! You sure had me fooled. I thought it was a natural nature scene! Good job!', '2006-07-04 18:43:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584860, 349502, 52713, '<td valign="top">First impression - Pretty flower, nice composition.<br/> <br/>This bokeh thing is difficult to capture. Most definitions of bokeh include some sort of out of focus highlights. However, the blue and the yellow ribbon winners didn''t really have that. So bokeh has evolved it seems to be something with out of focus elements that add to the composition. In that case, you were successful. The main flower is very sharp and the background completely blurred. <br/> <br/>The shadow falling on the middle of the flower probably takes a but of the impact away. Choosing a flower more in the light and shooting at a different time of day might have helped. The quality of light is excellent.<br/> <br/>This is a good shot of a pretty flower that is lacking a certain "wow" factor needed to score higher at DPC.<br/> <br/>I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions.<br/> <br/>David<br/></td>', 'First impression - Pretty flower, nice composition. This bokeh thing is difficult to capture. Most definitions of bokeh include some sort of out of focus highlights. However, the blue and the yellow ribbon winners didn''t really have that. So bokeh has evolved it seems to be something with out of focus elements that add to the composition. In that case, you were successful. The main flower is very sharp and the background completely blurred.  The shadow falling on the middle of the flower probably takes a but of the impact away. Choosing a flower more in the light and shooting at a different time of day might have helped. The quality of light is excellent. This is a good shot of a pretty flower that is lacking a certain "wow" factor needed to score higher at DPC. I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. David', '2006-07-04 18:43:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584903, 349482, 52713, '<td valign="top"><br/>I''ll bet you''re wondering why your butterfly came in 6th and another butterfly came in first.<br/> <br/>Your shot is composed very well. The square crop and main subject placement are very pleasing. As for the bokeh effect, there''s not really any out of focus highlights, but then there wasn''t any in the top finisher either.<br/> <br/>There''s not much to critique in this top 10 image. If I had to pick something that made a difference between this one and the top finisher it is the background. Yours a bit busy and fights for attention from the butterfly, albeit only slightly. The blade of grass coming in from the top is a bit on the over exposed side. I would have burned it down in the editing.<br/> <br/>Other than that, congratulations on your top 10 finish, and your new personal best by a long shot!<br/> <br/>I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions.<br/> <br/>David<br/></td>', 'I''ll bet you''re wondering why your butterfly came in 6th and another butterfly came in first. Your shot is composed very well. The square crop and main subject placement are very pleasing. As for the bokeh effect, there''s not really any out of focus highlights, but then there wasn''t any in the top finisher either. There''s not much to critique in this top 10 image. If I had to pick something that made a difference between this one and the top finisher it is the background. Yours a bit busy and fights for attention from the butterfly, albeit only slightly. The blade of grass coming in from the top is a bit on the over exposed side. I would have burned it down in the editing. Other than that, congratulations on your top 10 finish, and your new personal best by a long shot! I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. David', '2006-07-04 18:58:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2585571, 347928, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Shamrock, very nice image you have here.  And it scored comparatively well in this competitive crowd.  Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>I''ve studied your very good specimen carefully and really like what you have done to ''imortalize'' the creature.  I''m glad you found a way to secure the critter so you could get a good image.  Since it was just the shell, you could have taken the easy way and just picked the rosemary and brought him to a sheltered area.  You did it the hard way and that earns extra points in my book.<br/> <br/>Since this was a bokeh challenge, I''m going to be a little unorthodox here and suggest (after looking at this on my screen in many different cropping angles) that you might look at this again and crop say 1/8th to 1/4 of the image on the <strike>right</strike> <b>left, ooops, I meant to say left!</b> side.  It still leaves plenty of bokeh/background, but it does concentrate on that very well defined carapace.  Do you like it better?  Maybe so?  Maybe not?<br/> <br/>About the only other idea for changing (not necessarily improving) your image would be to play around with lighting so the underside of the carapace has a bit more light play.<br/> <br/>All this is beside the point. YOu have a good image and it scored well.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-12 00:28:44.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Shamrock, very nice image you have here.  And it scored comparatively well in this competitive crowd.  Keep up the good work. I''ve studied your very good specimen carefully and really like what you have done to ''imortalize'' the creature.  I''m glad you found a way to secure the critter so you could get a good image.  Since it was just the shell, you could have taken the easy way and just picked the rosemary and brought him to a sheltered area.  You did it the hard way and that earns extra points in my book. Since this was a bokeh challenge, I''m going to be a little unorthodox here and suggest (after looking at this on my screen in many different cropping angles) that you might look at this again and crop say 1/8th to 1/4 of the image on the right left, ooops, I meant to say left! side.  It still leaves plenty of bokeh/background, but it does concentrate on that very well defined carapace.  Do you like it better?  Maybe so?  Maybe not? About the only other idea for changing (not necessarily improving) your image would be to play around with lighting so the underside of the carapace has a bit more light play. All this is beside the point. YOu have a good image and it scored well.', '2006-07-05 00:03:24.000000', '2006-07-12 01:28:44.000000', 0),
(2585635, 349488, 60862, '<td valign="top">You''re very hard on yourself!  It''s a nice pic.  I wish my "horrible" efforts looked as good as yours. :)</td>', 'You''re very hard on yourself!  It''s a nice pic.  I wish my "horrible" efforts looked as good as yours. :)', '2006-07-05 00:24:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2585690, 350455, 47933, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club Sara!<br/> <br/>So sorry that your first image with us here did poorly because of resizing. It looks like your technicals were okay but it''s hard to tell much because of the pixelating issue. The flash might be a tad much as the flower looks to be a bit hot. I would certainly like to view the original so I could give you a valuable critique.<br/> <br/>Looking forward to seeing more of your entries and welcome to DPC Sara!<br/> <br/>Cheers - Phil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Sara! So sorry that your first image with us here did poorly because of resizing. It looks like your technicals were okay but it''s hard to tell much because of the pixelating issue. The flash might be a tad much as the flower looks to be a bit hot. I would certainly like to view the original so I could give you a valuable critique. Looking forward to seeing more of your entries and welcome to DPC Sara! Cheers - Phil', '2006-07-05 00:40:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2586794, 350732, 41337, '<td valign="top">I like the composition and the bokeh is good. Not sure about the noise and the white pixels seem a little strange to me. Would have done better if the flower was sharper and the image cleaner. I agree with Rebecca about the color but I''m ok with the amount of light you have here.</td>', 'I like the composition and the bokeh is good. Not sure about the noise and the white pixels seem a little strange to me. Would have done better if the flower was sharper and the image cleaner. I agree with Rebecca about the color but I''m ok with the amount of light you have here.', '2006-07-05 07:41:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2588437, 350723, 60396, '<td valign="top">Thank you for your comments.  They are proving to be really useful and I am now gaining some confidence in using different aspects of Photoshop to ''improve'' my pictures.</td>', 'Thank you for your comments.  They are proving to be really useful and I am now gaining some confidence in using different aspects of Photoshop to ''improve'' my pictures.', '2006-07-05 15:45:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2589077, 350958, 35334, '<td valign="top">Since you asked for comments, I''ll try to say something helpful. I have not read the comments that have already been made so I may repeat things that have already been said.<br/> <br/>I think it is a nice shot of the skink. I get a good sense of what the creature is like and I can almost feel him squirming around between the fingers. I think it would have been much better if you could have shown more of the skink. It would have been great if he could have been on top of or in front of the two fingers in the foreground.<br/> <br/>The out-of-focus background is nice--it is certainly not distracting from the animal. But I don''t think the bokeh is adding much either.<br/> <br/>I wish I could see the original. I have a feeling that the bokeh in green might add a sense of natural plant environment that would enhance the image. I''m also not fond of the partial desaturation. There is just enough color to make me start wondering about the color of the skink. I think I would prefer it in black and white. It is also possible that you could just turn down the green channel to take care of the excess and yet leave the hand and skink looking reasonably natural.<br/> <br/>--DanW</td>', 'Since you asked for comments, I''ll try to say something helpful. I have not read the comments that have already been made so I may repeat things that have already been said. I think it is a nice shot of the skink. I get a good sense of what the creature is like and I can almost feel him squirming around between the fingers. I think it would have been much better if you could have shown more of the skink. It would have been great if he could have been on top of or in front of the two fingers in the foreground. The out-of-focus background is nice--it is certainly not distracting from the animal. But I don''t think the bokeh is adding much either. I wish I could see the original. I have a feeling that the bokeh in green might add a sense of natural plant environment that would enhance the image. I''m also not fond of the partial desaturation. There is just enough color to make me start wondering about the color of the skink. I think I would prefer it in black and white. It is also possible that you could just turn down the green channel to take care of the excess and yet leave the hand and skink looking reasonably natural. --DanW', '2006-07-05 17:55:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2589387, 349755, 22975, '<td valign="top">this is great, love his expression!!</td>', 'this is great, love his expression!!', '2006-07-05 18:46:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2590701, 349217, 61632, '<td valign="top">WOOOOWWW I totally thought it was a real scene! Absolutly amazing!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-05 22:21:18.</i></td>', 'WOOOOWWW I totally thought it was a real scene! Absolutly amazing!', '2006-07-05 23:21:03.000000', '2006-07-05 23:21:18.000000', 0),
(2592814, 349697, 8367, '<td valign="top">A stunning capture with beautiful lighting.<br/>Congratulations on your ribbon!</td>', 'A stunning capture with beautiful lighting.Congratulations on your ribbon!', '2006-07-06 10:37:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2594270, 351062, 22301, '<td valign="top">I would have made sure to to use the whole 150 kb limit, this is 54 kb, which means your file could have nearly been three times as large(with respect to detail). Take a look at this <a href="//dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tutorial</a> if you you use photo shop.  I also think alittle bit of color in the image would have helped your score and some sort of noise reduction software like neat image or if you don''t want to download the free version you can try using gaussian blur and fade the amount in the opacity.  You have some good images in your portfolio but I think they need alittle work on post processing and if you look through the tutorials they can be a huge help. I know they helped me out alot. Hope this helps you.</td>', 'I would have made sure to to use the whole 150 kb limit, this is 54 kb, which means your file could have nearly been three times as large(with respect to detail). Take a look at this tutorial if you you use photo shop.  I also think alittle bit of color in the image would have helped your score and some sort of noise reduction software like neat image or if you don''t want to download the free version you can try using gaussian blur and fade the amount in the opacity.  You have some good images in your portfolio but I think they need alittle work on post processing and if you look through the tutorials they can be a huge help. I know they helped me out alot. Hope this helps you.', '2006-07-06 18:01:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2596975, 350068, 48928, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot :) I love orchids and this is a good one.</td>', 'Very nice shot :) I love orchids and this is a good one.', '2006-07-07 11:19:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2597148, 350068, 15711, '<td valign="top">You did so well with this.  Congrats on top 25.</td>', 'You did so well with this.  Congrats on top 25.', '2006-07-07 12:08:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2597531, 348584, 60799, '<td valign="top">That butterfly has some amazing colors happening between the reds and the greens.  I''ve been to a few different butterfly habitats and never come across anything like that.</td>', 'That butterfly has some amazing colors happening between the reds and the greens.  I''ve been to a few different butterfly habitats and never come across anything like that.', '2006-07-07 14:07:48.000000', NULL, 0),
