(2636652, 349276, 34192, '<td valign="top">Okay, typically I like chickens.  I really like all barnyard animals.  They are so cool!  But this one is really rather ugly.  No, he''s really ugly.</td>', 'Okay, typically I like chickens.  I really like all barnyard animals.  They are so cool!  But this one is really rather ugly.  No, he''s really ugly.', '2006-07-19 09:13:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639587, 349909, 50578, '<td valign="top">we have an 8 month old son,  nothing beats a sleeping baby.  you captured a nice moment.  I think the angle you used works well.  But i disagree with you on the bears, I think they should be sharper instead of blurred more.  hard to get both when you want to get a close up of your subject though, at least from my own experience...  <br/>nice pic.</td>', 'we have an 8 month old son,  nothing beats a sleeping baby.  you captured a nice moment.  I think the angle you used works well.  But i disagree with you on the bears, I think they should be sharper instead of blurred more.  hard to get both when you want to get a close up of your subject though, at least from my own experience...  nice pic.', '2006-07-19 19:47:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639953, 350553, 57358, '<td valign="top">wow, you got a ton of comments on this pic, but what''s one more?  love this shot... very movie-esk...  only thing I might change, BG permitting, would be to add more space to the top and left sides, great color and sharp focus</td>', 'wow, you got a ton of comments on this pic, but what''s one more?  love this shot... very movie-esk...  only thing I might change, BG permitting, would be to add more space to the top and left sides, great color and sharp focus', '2006-07-19 21:39:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639999, 349739, 20530, '<td valign="top">I fall into the camp of people who find the flower in foreground a bit distracting. I feel this way because I''m so interested in the great detail and gorgeous colors going on right behind it. I can''t say enough about how much I like the range and vibrancy of the colors!<br/> <br/>I do appreciate the unique approach at composition. The shape and scale of the flower in FG is repeated by the tree in BG which creates a sense of balance. As well as the diagonal placement of those elements, which makes a dynamic composition.<br/> <br/>You have clearly striven to define BOKEH with this image; and although I''m not crazy about the white "blob", I do think you have succeeded.</td>', 'I fall into the camp of people who find the flower in foreground a bit distracting. I feel this way because I''m so interested in the great detail and gorgeous colors going on right behind it. I can''t say enough about how much I like the range and vibrancy of the colors! I do appreciate the unique approach at composition. The shape and scale of the flower in FG is repeated by the tree in BG which creates a sense of balance. As well as the diagonal placement of those elements, which makes a dynamic composition. You have clearly striven to define BOKEH with this image; and although I''m not crazy about the white "blob", I do think you have succeeded.', '2006-07-19 21:47:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2642091, 350068, 32754, '<td valign="top">this wet orchid is just lovely...the background is perfect bokeh.</td>', 'this wet orchid is just lovely...the background is perfect bokeh.', '2006-07-20 11:40:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2642170, 350237, 48228, '<td valign="top">I made a comment on this one in the challenge, but I like to add some more in depth ones now. I actuallly do really like this a lot, and feel to definately suited the challenge. I think the focus on the one daisy works so well, and the background is just so colorful..... Good jod.</td>', 'I made a comment on this one in the challenge, but I like to add some more in depth ones now. I actuallly do really like this a lot, and feel to definately suited the challenge. I think the focus on the one daisy works so well, and the background is just so colorful..... Good jod.', '2006-07-20 12:09:19.000000', NULL, 0),
